; error: 8:14: 'f' is given a lambda that may send back what fixed 'xs' owns, and nothing changes through what a fixed name owns; make 'f' fixed, or have the lambda send back a copy, as in '<- xs.copy() at r'
; A lambda that sends back what it keeps of a fixed name can't be kept by a
; flex name, which would give a flex name what the lambda sends back.

task main()
    region r
    fixed xs = [1, 2, ...] at r
    flex f = [@r]() -> [int]@r <- xs fi
    show(f())
fi
